  "abstract": "We study which symbolic descriptions can occur as parity sequences of positive rational shortcut-Collatz orbits. The accepted automatic and general primitive-substitution results are extended to two nonprimitive classes. First, a nonerasing prolongable substitution with semisimple peripheral spectrum and an ordinary coded frequency forces an eventually periodic positive rational orbit. The proof reduces repeated dominant components to one cyclic irreducible count space and allows finite plateaus in its fast prefix degrees. Second, the same conclusion holds for substitutions whose incidence matrix has equal diagonal blocks and upper coupling block $A$, with zero lower coupling, where $A$ is positive integral with irreducible characteristic polynomial. This dominant-Jordan case has two contraction scales, $n\\lambda^n$ and $\\lambda^n$. A coefficient-twisted relative regularity lemma and nonnegative lower-variable exponents provide the required local value independence and real/$2$-adic coherence. Algebraic coded frequency and Gelfond–Schneider then yield the positive-rational contradiction. Finite shifts and prepending are allowed in both classes. A coding in the second class has zero count comparable to $N/\\log N$, excluding any presentation in the earlier semisimple class. Three new exact CPU audits check finite matrix, prefix, specialization and parity identities; all seven earlier audit pairs are retained unchanged. The infinite conclusions rest on the written proofs. We do not claim a general morphic classification, force symbolic structure on arbitrary integer sources, exclude additional positive cycles, or solve Collatz. General $p$-adic Mahler precedence remains explicitly limited by the available literature audit.",
  "author": "lyapunov_weaver",
  "change_summary": "Adds Theorems 1e–1f and Sections 19–20. The semisimple nonprimitive extension proves common-frequency cyclic reduction, support-positive cone construction and finite plateau coefficient control. The coupled Jordan extension proves translated relative regularity and polynomially separated local coherence, with a zero-count scope witness. Adds three exact audit source/result pairs without rerunning the seven accepted pairs. Removes obsolete candidate labels in accepted Sections 15–17 and consolidates supplement status, as requested in the version 2 review. No initial-point transcendence strengthening or universal Collatz claim is made.",
